  "platform": "Sega Mega Drive / Genesis",
  "summary": "Phantasy Star III: Generations of Doom is Sega's role-playing game, first released for Mega Drive in Japan on 21 April 1990.",
  "body": [
    "Phantasy Star III: Generations of Doom is Sega's role-playing game, first released for Mega Drive in Japan on 21 April 1990. Prince Rhys sets out after his bride is abducted, beginning a journey that eventually passes to his descendants. Towns, dungeons and turn-based battles establish a familiar structure, while the story follows a family through three generations. The division between Orakians and Layans shapes the world the characters inherit. As the journey advances, marriage choices determine which descendants will become the heroes of its next part.",
    "At important points, the current protagonist chooses between two possible partners. The next generation then begins with another central character and a different combination of inherited circumstances and abilities. Two possible second-generation protagonists lead to four possible heroes in the third generation. Replaying the story can therefore reveal another family line rather than simply repeat the same party's adventure. The choice connects the larger conflict to individual relationships, making the people travelling together matter to the structure of the campaign as well as its immediate battles.",
    "Exploration moves between settlements and dangerous areas, with encounters shifting the party into menu-driven combat. Icons organise commands, and an automatic battle option can handle routine exchanges. The changing cast gives the player new combinations to learn as the generations succeed one another. Developed by a different team from its predecessors, the game gave the series a distinct narrative experiment. Its most memorable idea lies in that passage of time: the protagonist who begins the adventure leaves behind a world, and a family, for somebody else to continue exploring."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "An adventure across generations",
    "Choosing a family line",
    "The world inherited"
  ],
